-- A per-cell neural read on a structural walk down a list of Symbols: the
-- recursion's argument (tail xs) decreases, and the read's input (head xs) is
-- a point, yet walk's probability is refused by requireDeterministicUnderEnum
-- ("draws fresh randomness by calling walk_gen, which is on a recursive call
-- cycle"), and `compile` silently emits generate-only code. This is the
-- shape of a recursive-descent parser over handwritten glyphs that reads each
-- cell when it consumes it; the only admitted spelling reads every cell up
-- front, which enumerates all 16^N readings per query. Found by
-- experiments_nest handwritten-arithmetic-roundtrip (docs task
-- exp-handwritten-arithmetic-roundtrip), verified at f16f701 on dev. Ticket
-- decreasing-recursion-refused-as-generate-fallback (addendum 2026-10-26).
-- Idealized: p(True) = glyph(x0)[1] * glyph(x1)[1] = 0.5 * 0.6 = 0.3.
expect-failure: refused "which is on a recursive call cycle"
